WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.310
Endless.

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:06.470
That’s a word you’re likely to hear thrown
around a lot at the SCP Foundation.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:10.450
Like SCP-3008, known as the Infinite Ikea.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:11.590
Endless.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:17.679
Or take the life of the tragically immortal
Dr. Bright, who became one with the SCP-963,

00:00:17.679 --> 00:00:21.890
and now is condemned to existing within it
on some level forever.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:22.890
Endless.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:29.880
Or most pertinent of all for today’s video,
take SCP-087, a terrifying staircase full

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.340
of tangible darkness and a frightening and
unknowable entity.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:39.820
No matter how far down you go, it seems as
though there’s just another flight, waiting

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.200
for you.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.200
Endless.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.290
But really, is anything ever really endless?

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:49.680
Or is endless just the word we use for something
when we haven’t found that sought-after

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.050
end just yet?

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:55.100
For those who travel far enough, there may
be a limit to the infinite Ikea.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:00.660
Someday, Dr. Bright’s medallion one day
might lay inert and lifeless, with no traces

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.570
of his consciousness left.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:07.240
And for those who venture down far enough,
able to clench their teeth and get past the

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:13.109
fear, you may someday find that even SCP-087
has a final flight.

00:01:13.109 --> 00:01:15.770
But what if this isn’t just a hypothetical.

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:20.259
What if this has already happened, but the
truth was considered too dangerous or too

00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:21.960
horrifying to share?

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.840
What’s really at the bottom of SCP-087?

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.399
Today, we hope to find out.

00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:32.450
Let’s just also hope that knowing doesn’t
end up being more of a burden than we’d

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.450
expected…

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.000
Before we head to the bottom of the Endless
Staircase though, we must first return to

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.109
SCP-087’s file and refresh our memories
on some of the crucial basics.

00:01:42.109 --> 00:01:45.929
After all, it’s been quite some time since
our last video on the subject.

00:01:45.929 --> 00:01:50.819
This Euclid-Class anomaly is one of the most
well-known and feared, partially thanks to

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:56.100
classified information being leaked via a
certain video game, probably coded by the

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.179
Serpent’s Hand.

00:01:57.179 --> 00:02:03.420
As we alluded to earlier, many know 087 as
the Endless Staircase, based in an administrative

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.880
building of a classified North American university
campus.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.790
It’s been behind a number of mysterious
deaths and disappearances and has left many

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:16.650
of its escaping victims traumatized and in
a state of permanent catatonia.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.299
Having to descend the staircase is just that
terrifying.

00:02:20.299 --> 00:02:25.530
Equally infamous as the staircase itself are
the three tests that the Foundation conducted

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:29.280
into the staircase before deciding to just
board up the door forever.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.430
In the first, a D-Class that was once a member
of the Foundation was forced to see just how

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:36.439
many flights he could descend.

00:02:36.439 --> 00:02:40.650
Not long after first entering the staircase
and beginning to make his way down, he heard

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.829
the desperate and distressed pleas of a child.

00:02:43.829 --> 00:02:48.110
He kept descending but found he seemed to
be getting no closer to the source of the

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.110
distress.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:55.760
When he was deep enough, that’s when he
encountered SCP-087-1, a frightening, uncanny

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.760
face with few discernible features.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:03.170
The sheer terror of encountering this entity
was enough to send him running back to the

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:04.170
top.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:08.810
The second test played out similarly, with
a D-Class being sent in with a number of powerful,

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:13.510
sticky-backed lights that he was ordered to
place against the walls as he descended.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:16.920
This was done in hopes of increasing visibility
on the staircase.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:22.510
However, it proved to be unsuccessful, as
the darkness in 087 is more of a tangible

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:25.390
presence than the mere absence of light.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:29.930
It was able to smother out visibility regardless
of a light source’s power.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:36.000
Once again, the D-Class heard the crying,
and encountered the face, causing him to flee.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.969
And the third and penultimate test involved
a D-Class who got really unlucky.

00:03:40.969 --> 00:03:45.990
She traversed the staircase deeper than any
of her predecessors, before eventually encountering

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.640
the horrifying face of SCP-087-1.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:54.609
However, rather than running up and away from
the entity, in a state of sheer panic, the

00:03:54.609 --> 00:03:59.980
D-Class instead ran downwards, deeper and
deeper into the staircase.

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:06.019
The audio cut as the face continued in its
pursuit, and the D-Class was never seen again.

00:04:06.019 --> 00:04:10.550
Did you notice that we said “penultimate”
and not “final” before that last one?

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:16.230
That’s because there’s actually a highly
classified fourth expedition into the SCP-087

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:22.079
Staircase, but as you can see on the original
file, the data is expunged.

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:26.669
What could have happened in that study that
led the Foundation to wipe it from the records?

00:04:26.669 --> 00:04:32.400
Did they discover the great secret behind
SCP-087, a secret too horrible for mortal

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:33.750
minds to bear?

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:38.590
We’re not just going to give you one answer
today, we’re going to give you three.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:45.830
That’s right: Three different interpretations
of the secret fourth expedition into SCP-087.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:47.050
Which is the real one?

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.960
Well you’ll just have to see.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:54.100
After all, nothing is simple when it comes
to SCP-087.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:57.820
Though our first potential option is the most
simple of the three.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:02.520
In this iteration of the experiment, a male
D-Class murderer was instructed to descend

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:08.349
the staircase into the heart of SCP-087, with
the Foundation hoping to find out what happened

00:05:08.349 --> 00:05:14.370
to D-9884, the female D-Class who’d disappeared
at the conclusion of the third expedition.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:20.539
In a sense, this new D-Class would discover
the fate that most likely befell D-9884, but

00:05:20.539 --> 00:05:24.729
through first-hand experience rather than
distant observation.

00:05:24.729 --> 00:05:30.030
Being directed by Dr. Airdo over walkie-talkie,
the male D-Class slowly got deeper into the

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:32.620
anomaly, flight by flight.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:36.970
Predictably, he began to hear the intensely
distressed crying of a small child around

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:42.870
200 meters below him and immediately felt
a sense of paranoia and dread wash over his

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:43.870
mind.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:48.880
Despite this, Dr. Airdo ordered him to keep
going, descending deeper and deeper into the

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.970
bowels of SCP-087.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:57.120
Over time, the sheer psychological exhaustion
of SCP-087 was beginning to take its toll

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:01.400
on the D-Class, leading to him taking a brief
break in order to nap.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:08.250
However, he awoke with a violent start, seeing
the horrific face of SCP-087-1 staring down

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.250
at him.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:12.750
It felt like all his worst nightmares had
come to life.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:18.620
In order to escape the monster, he began to
flee further down into SCP-087, much like

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:20.990
D-9884 before him.

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:24.430
It would be the last mistake he ever made.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:29.639
When he finally reached the very bottom of
the 087 staircases, the D-Class realized he

00:06:29.639 --> 00:06:30.900
was trapped.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.419
Nowhere to run, nowhere to hide.

00:06:33.419 --> 00:06:40.190
Suddenly, the face of SCP-087-1 was hovering
over him again, boring its gaze into him.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:45.061
As the D-Class directed his powerful flashlight
at the creature, he saw that this time, it

00:06:45.061 --> 00:06:47.460
was more than just a face.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:53.720
The entity had a whole body, seven or eight
feet long, with that same ghostly white and

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.180
deathlike appearance.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:59.430
It reached out with huge, clawed hands and
grasped the D-Class.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:03.810
Before the audio and video feed cut out entirely,
the last thing the attending researchers heard

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:08.690
was screaming from the hapless D-Class, and
the crunch of his bones within the creature’s

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.240
huge hands.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.750
But of course, that’s just one of three
possible insane discoveries at the very bottom

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:15.830
of SCP-087.

00:07:15.830 --> 00:07:22.320
Let’s turn our attention to the next one,
and see if its answer to the SCP-087 riddle

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:25.860
seems to satisfy all of our burning questions.

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:30.530
Much like the previous iteration, a single
male D-Class was sent into the clutches of

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:36.960
SCP-087 in hopes of getting some answers on
what happened to D-9884.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:41.810
Of course, he was given all the standard equipment
- from a 75-watt flashlight to a defensive

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:46.039
weapon to a healthy supply of water and nutrition
bars.

00:07:46.039 --> 00:07:48.490
None of which would save him in the end.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:54.530
Like all the others, this D-Class descended
those accursed stairs, getting deeper and

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:55.530
deeper.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:08:00.419
When he reached a certain point on the way
down, he heard something, but not the crying

00:08:00.419 --> 00:08:03.030
of a child like all the others had reported.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:06.030
It was an adult woman’s scream.

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:12.389
Specifically, it was the scream of D-9884,
exactly as the Foundation researchers had

00:08:12.389 --> 00:08:17.169
heard it over the audio feed in her last moments
before disappearing.

00:08:17.169 --> 00:08:18.659
This was progress.

00:08:18.659 --> 00:08:23.470
The researchers instructed this male D-Class
to go deeper, passing flight after flight,

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:27.759
until finally the SCP-087-1 face appeared.

00:08:27.759 --> 00:08:31.750
But again, something was different, something
was wrong.

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:38.039
Now, it looked more like the face of D-9884,
just without her mouth and pupils.

00:08:38.039 --> 00:08:42.459
Had SCP-087-1 been stealing the faces of its
prior victims?

00:08:42.459 --> 00:08:47.580
Had the previous face been stolen from a student
who’d gone missing from the campus?

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:52.390
These were all questions the male D-Class
didn’t have time to ponder, as he was too

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:54.600
busy running for dear life.

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.250
But he didn’t get far.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:09:00.920
Despite having no history of such medical
problems, the male D-Class suddenly experienced

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:04.570
a seizure while attempting to escape, and
collapsed.

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:09.089
The last thing his video feed picked up before
losing transmission was a pair of long, white

00:09:09.089 --> 00:09:14.709
arms emerging from the dark, crushing him
inside of its huge hands, before dragging

00:09:14.709 --> 00:09:17.140
his enfolded corpse into the darkness.

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:22.640
That’s another chilling potential account
of the possible fourth expedition into SCP-087,

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:25.329
but we can’t stop now.

00:09:25.329 --> 00:09:30.060
We still have one more tale of terror to share
before this video is done.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:36.410
In the next and final iteration, two D-Classes
- one male and one female - were sent down

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:40.980
together in hopes of discovering what had
happened to D-9884.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:46.470
And by the end, they would have their answer,
but they certainly wouldn’t like it.

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:50.610
As the two of them descended, they saw the
marks on the wall where the adhesive lights

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.960
from expedition two had been somehow torn
off.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:58.779
But the deeper they descended, the more disturbing
the things they found became.

00:09:58.779 --> 00:10:03.610
They discovered words clawed into the stone
walls, each one revealing a piece of a more

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:07.110
frightening puzzle the deeper down SCP-087
they traversed.

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:13.180
They descended further, sustaining minor injuries
from a foul-smelling and caustic substance

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:16.120
left on some of the walls and floors around
them.

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:21.610
At some point along the journey, a light was
dropped, and in the brief seconds of darkness,

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:23.810
the female D-Class disappeared.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:28.250
The male D-Class was ordered to go deeper
and deeper into the staircase until he finally

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:31.320
began to hear the crying of a little girl.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:38.020
When he reached the 666th floor, he found
a wooden door, with the word “HOME” scratched

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:39.020
into it.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:42.060
He steeled himself and entered the room.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:48.170
But it wasn’t a room at all, it was a field,
shrouded in darkness with a distant tree.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:53.490
A little girl - the one who had been crying
- was finally, actually here.

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:57.870
She told the D-Class that she’d always been
here, and her father had been trying to find

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:03.040
her a body so she could go “upstairs”,
but for that to happen, she’d have to be

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.010
properly birthed first.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:10.800
That’s when the male D-Class noticed the
two huge stone slabs just beyond the darkness:

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:17.190
On one was the corpse of D-9884, hanged by
her wrists with thick, metal chains.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:22.720
Her abdomen had been fully cut open, as though
a brutal c-section had been performed on her.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:28.010
And on the other stone was the female D-Class
who’d been accompanying him this whole time,

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:33.570
strung up but still very much alive - seemingly
the next potential vessel for the little girl’s

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:34.570
rebirth.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:39.380
But this didn’t mean that the male D-Class
would be left out of the fun, either.

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:44.260
After all, the little girl’s father would
need a new body, too, if he wanted to accompany

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.190
his daughter upstairs.

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:52.910
The father in question being SCP-087-1, which
appeared in the room moments later and swooped

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:55.250
in towards the male D-Class.

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:59.860
What followed was a battery of nightmarish
sounds as the darkness expanded and consumed

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.889
the field once more.

00:12:01.889 --> 00:12:07.930
Not long after this, the Foundation sealed
off the entrance to SCP-087 forever, now knowing

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:12.959
that it potentially contained multiple hostile
entities intent on escaping into our world

00:12:12.959 --> 00:12:15.410
and causing further damage.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:18.940
Students in the area reported a number of
frantic knocks coming from the door for a

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:24.271
brief period after that until the Foundation
finally had it properly soundproofed, and

00:12:24.271 --> 00:12:26.889
the issues were seemingly over with.

00:12:26.889 --> 00:12:27.920
For now.

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:33.889
So there you have it: Three potential terrifying
secrets at the bottom of SCP-087.

00:12:33.889 --> 00:12:35.769
Which do you think is the most likely?

00:12:35.769 --> 00:12:37.740
Let us know down in the comments.

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:44.640
After all, when it comes to SCP-087, it seems
you can always delve just a little bit deeper...

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:50.440
Now go check out “SCP-3008 - Trapped in
IKEA” and “SCP-049 - the Plague Doctor

00:12:50.440 --> 00:12:53.470
Captured” for more classic SCPs from SCP
Explained!

